cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this index in your work, please cite it as below. Developed by Zhenxian LI with assistance from Claude Codex."
type: dataset
title: "Psychoacoustic Metrics Index"
abstract: >-
  A curated, weekly-refreshed index of open-source implementations of psychoacoustic metrics in any
  programming language: loudness, sharpness, roughness, fluctuation strength, tonality, impulsiveness and
  psychoacoustic annoyance, with related quantities such as equal-loudness contours, effective perceived
  noise level (EPNL) and aural detectability. Each implementation is listed under the standard edition or
  model paper it follows (for example ISO 532-1, ECMA-418-2 or DIN 45692), together with its licence,
  packages, release activity and the validation evidence the project itself states. The index consists of
  data and a static website; it contains no metric code and does not run the indexed software.
authors:
  - given-names: Zhenxian
    family-names: LI
    alias: ZhenxianLi
keywords:
  - psychoacoustics
  - psychoacoustic metrics
  - sound quality
  - loudness
  - sharpness
  - roughness
  - fluctuation strength
  - tonality
  - ISO 532
  - ECMA-418
  - DIN 45692
  - open source software
  - index
license: MIT
